==Strategy==
With a strong and synergistic [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] army, No Return Flights is one of the hardest stages in Stories of Legend. It is advised to boost your units past Lv.30 for this reason.

Waves of Otta-smack-us spawn in intervals throughout the stage. Stall those Otta-smack-u waves in the startoff to max out your [[Worker Cat]] and stockpile as much cash as possible; you will most likely need it given how harsh the stage is on cash. Once your cat army hits the enemy base, you are greeted by Dolphinas—who debut in the stage—buffed Rain Ds, and the boss of the stage, a massively buffed Master A.

Dolphina has fast movement speed and high health. You'll notice her short standing range of 150 is within her blind spot, but this is by design. Dolphina will start her attack once your meatshields enter her range, but the actual attack hits further back, right where your backliners will be. Dolphina is weak to your melee and lower-end midranged units, but this weakness is covered by the Rain Ds, who have the strength to destroy just about anything with under 300 range. And while both of these enemies have many knockbacks to let you juggle them, you will inevitably end up pushing into the Master A., who will make quick work of anything that enters his range. With how much damage is being showered across the whole battlefield, expect every cat you bring to die after a while and instead focus on extracting as much value out of them as possible. This stage is also dry on cash, meaning you have to manage your money carefully. As a rule of thumb, try to ensure you have at least 4500¢, as finding the perfect moment to summon [[Awakened Bahamut Cat]] is difficult yet crucial.

With this stage heavily discouraging heavy, sustainable backline units due to the aforementioned pressure, your loadout should instead focus on cost-effective melee/midranged units that can fit in Dolphina's blind spot and are powerful yet disposable. Bringing backliners with 650 range or less is ill-advised due to Dolphina's [[Long Distance]] attacks, but snipers with more range than that, like [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Cat]] are welcome. Additionally, No Return Flights was released when the only specialist [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless cat]] was [[Shadow Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Shadow Gao]], so anti-Traitless cats offer a significant amount of powercreep to the stage, and are especially useful for {{4c}}.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Awakened Bahamut Cat is difficult to time due to the nature of the stage, but is pretty much mandatory here due to his immense burst damage being able to turn the tide. His [[Explosion]] [[Talents|Talent]] increases his destructive power and is very useful for higher crown difficulties.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Can Cat possesses incredible stats for a mere 675¢, allowing them to get immense value in just one hit. Their Extra Bounties Talent can be very helpful in a cash-dry stage like this, while their Move Speed Up Talent help with timing them to avoid Dolphina's attacks. Overall, very useful to have.
*[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]]: Cameraman Cat's slow movement speed is annoying, but she can still gun down the Dolphinas and Otta-smack-us if she can sneak into Dolphina's blindspot, offering great damage.
*[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]]: While there are no [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien enemies]] here, Seafarer Cat's strong mid-ranged DPS, good HP, fair cost and high speed help him be useful against the Otta-smack-us and Dolphinas, but do be wary of his lengthy cooldown.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]: Similarly to Seafarer Cat, Pizza Cat is a strong midranger whose generalist stats help him be a big help against the enemy frontline even without any [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark enemies]] in this stage. His slow speed and long cooldown are issues, however.
*[[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]]: When boosted to Lv. 40, Cyborg Cat becomes one of the best choices for the stage. She is easily stackable, outranges Rain D., can easily juggle both Dolphina and Rain D., and can still fit in Dolphina's blind spot if you are careful with your meatshielding.
*[[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]]: Using the enemy frontliners as stepping stones, Housewife Cat can juggle the Rain Ds and chip down the Master A. She becomes even better with her [[Savage Blow]] Talent unlocked.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]: While Hacker Cat is already good here, Cyberpunk Cat breaks this stage in half due to his immense range and guaranteed Slow. By stalling Otta-smack-us at the start of the stage, you can stack up an army of Cyberpunk Cats who will permanently Slow the enemies of the stage for an easy win.
*[[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]]: Manic Macho Legs' [[Wave Attack]] is very helpful for chipping down the enemies, particularly Master A. and the Rain Ds.
*[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Teacher BearCat]]: While admittedly difficult to use, Teacher BearCat offers incredible frontline damage when timed well. Though, due to how hard he is to [[Flow Like the Stream (Merciless)|obtain]], you will likely only be using him for higher crown difficulties.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat Cat]]: A major source of power creep for this stage, Jellycat offers a devastating Wave Attack for a cheap price, being one of the best units here. It requires good timing, though its range increase in True Form makes that easier.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: The king of powercreep strikes again, using their disposable damage output and Long Distance pierce to get lots of value.
*[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]]: Haniwa Cat is an incredible meatshield here, as it is cheap, resists all enemies in this stage, and has slow speed to not easily be a stepping stone for Dolphina.
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]]: Hitman Cat's devastating anti-Traitless offense reduces the stage to rubble, though good luck [[Archaeology 401: Analysis|unlocking]] Hitman Cat before beating Stories of Legend on 1 crown.
*[[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]]: If you haven't beaten No Return Flights' higher crown difficulties by the time you unlock him, Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr. will ensure that is no longer the case. His powerful anti-Traitless stats and Knockback will destroy the stage.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Any [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] Uber will be immensely helpful here due to their focus on Traitless. While [[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Bane]] and [[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Doom Phono]] aren't anti-Traitless specialists per se, their ridiculous stats should still be able to carry you.
*[[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Issun Boshi/Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru]]: This anti-Traitless [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|Ultra Soul]] can be very helpful here. Issun Boshi is like an improved Teacher BearCat, while Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru is a strong rusher that can burst a ton of damage against the Traitless enemies here.

