==Trivia==
*No Return Flights and [[Dolphina]] both reference folk singer [[wikipedia:ja:イルカ (歌手)|Toshie "Iruka" Kanbe]], whose stage name means "dolphin":
**No Return Flights' Japanese name, Mō Riku ni wa Kaerenai (もう陸には帰れない, "Can't Return to Land Anymore"), is a play on "[https://youtu.be/x-JJ5NJXvt4 Mō Umi ni wa Kaerenai]" (もう海には帰れない, "Can't Return to Sea Anymore").
**Dolphina's description pulls from the [[wikipedia:Kaguyahime (band)|Kaguyahime]] song "[https://youtu.be/3-y-VregNqg Nagoriyuki]", which was famously [https://youtu.be/FwXluXjBaqw covered] by Iruka; it mentions riding a train, a careless youth, and wasting time without realizing it. Her Japanese description even says she rode the train from Tokyo.

